    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0028" n="22" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg22"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./97a: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                            Chiefs of Diplomatic Missions in the American
                            Republics
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-08T16:00:00-04:00">September 8,
                            1939—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President has announced that the Under Secretary of State<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d42-f1"/> will represent the United States at the conference in
                    Panama. He will be assisted by the following as advisers: The Honorable Edwin C.
                    Wilson, Minister Designate to Uruguay; and Dr. Herbert Feis,<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d42-f2"/> Dr. Warren Kelchner,<anchor n="14" xml:id="d42-f3"/> and
                    Miss Marjorie M. Whiteman,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d42-f4"/> of the Department of
                    State. Mr. Paul C. Daniels, Foreign Service Officer, will act as secretary to
                    Mr. Welles.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d42-f5"/>
                </p>
                <p>You will please inform the Government to which you are accredited.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d42-f1" n="12" xml:id="d42-f1-content">
                <p>Sumner Welles, Representative of the Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f2" n="13" xml:id="d42-f2-content">
                <p>Herbert Feis, Adviser; Adviser on International Economic Affairs, Department of
                    State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f3" n="14" xml:id="d42-f3-content">
                <p>Warren Kelchner, Secretary General of the Delegation: Chief, Division of
                    International Conferences, Department of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f4" n="15" xml:id="d42-f4-content">
                <p>Marjorie M. Whiteman, Legal Adviser; Assistant to the Legal Adviser, Department
                    of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f5" n="16" xml:id="d42-f5-content">
                <p>For a complete list of the delegation of the United States, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Report of the Delegate of the United States of America
                        to the Meeting of the Foreign Ministers of the American Republics Held at
                        Panamá September 23–October 8, 1939</hi> (Washington, Government Printing
                    Office, 1940).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
